# [O-29] pcrec-bench 2026-09-16, the `variant` TWIN of
# `o29_multi_provenance.rxtin`. Same mechanism, same three closing
# sites (blank line / comment line / end of file), same reason: `S0`'s
# "a BLANK and a COMMENT each close every open attachment" used to skip
# `RXT_CLOSE_FRAME` (and therefore `close_section_frame`) entirely via a
# raw `ndepth = 1` reset, so a `variant` sub-block that is the last
# content before a blank or comment line never reached
# `#section variants` — only the textually LAST block's variant survived,
# because only IT closes at end of file, the one site that was never
# broken.
#
# `variant <testee>`'s cardinality is REPEAT/`unique-by value` — distinct
# per block — so each block's testee differs from its own siblings (there
# are none here) and need not differ across blocks; kept distinct anyway
# for readability. `unsupported <reason>` satisfies the VARIANT schema's
# "exactly-one-of text unsupported" constraint with the simpler of the two
# LINE-shaped alternatives.
pattern p1 a
variant re2
  unsupported no per-engine spelling preserves the objective

pattern p2 b
variant tre
  unsupported no per-engine spelling preserves the objective
# a comment, not a blank line, separates block 2 from block 3
pattern p3 c
variant onig
  unsupported no per-engine spelling preserves the objective
